25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have plenty of coders, but the phenotyping experts have vanished. Also, our senior analysts are currently abroad.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Computing is free now, which is great! But shipping costs are up, even if the glasshouse subsidy is still there.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The data catalogues have lasted much longer than the mechanism studies. Also, breeding colonies cause the most delays.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"This is a mess. Field sites are being hit by fire and floods, and the spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The animal facility is finally stable with vet cover, but the glasshouses are completely full for two cycles.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, if the glasshouses are full, does that make the staffing strength there irrelevant?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, eleven weeks is a long time! Does that mean any project needing spectroscopy is a huge risk?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, if the technical staff are gone, maybe we should avoid the complex biological projects?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Daisuke, exactly. And if field sites are burning down, we can't rely on outdoor samples right now.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, no, the crew is there, but the space is gone. We cannot fit more plants in.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,It sounds like we should favor projects that rely on computation or stable indoor environments.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, if the glasshouses are full, then the drought signaling project might be in trouble, right?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. The breeding colony risk also makes the amphibian study look dangerous.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, yes. And the spectroscopy failure makes the protein folding study a gamble.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Minako,,Correct. The infrastructure simply cannot support the plant or protein projects currently.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Servas,,We are narrowing it down. We need something that uses the available coders and the stable repository.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Sakura,,The microbiome atlas sounds safe if it's mostly about sequences and metadata!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"And catalogues are the ones that actually provide long-term value, according to the closeout files.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Takumi,,It avoids the broken spectroscopy and the flooded field sites if the samples are already collected.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Minako,,"It fits the current capacity. The repository is fast now, so the data will actually be published.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
